Ramp windowed plays to the volume a volume command sets

The audio thread applied SetVolumeMatching to active_samples only, so a
`volume` aimed at a windowed play (mode "stream", or a file long or
large enough for auto to window) changed nothing audible while
/status/samples reported the new volume. Since carry-over, a volume
sent while such a play was still loading did apply, as its start
volume, so the result depended on whether the load had finished.

StreamedSource now has a target_volume beside its volume and ramps the
two together per frame (advance_volumes, using the same ramp_toward as
samples, which also replaces its hand-written voice-volume ramp), and
SetVolumeMatching sets the target of every matching streamed source as
it does for samples. A carried volume still becomes the start volume.

docs/bugs.md keeps only the seek half of the entry; command-ordering.md
no longer lists this as a difference; the CHANGELOG has a Fixed entry.
The README's feature list mentions starting a sound at a speed.

